{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"The target asserts that 'extreme value statistics ensure that catastrophic shared causes eventually dominate any topology' and that decentralization's resilience advantage is purely an 'observer bias' artifact. This conflates epistemic visibility of correlation with causal independence. The problem asks what evidence would distinguish failures that are genuinely independent from failures that merely appear uncorrelated until a shared cause is found. The target's mechanism (operators do not pool failure data, correlation is never recognized) addresses only the detection side. But detection failure does not change actual failure rates or recovery properties. Consider geographic separation: if one decentralized operator is down due to a regional flood, another in a different region may fail for an unrelated reason at the same time, yet the network as a whole still serves traffic. In the centralized system, the same flood takes the entire large service offline because it is co-located. Here the shared cause does not 'dominate' the distributed topology — it is attenuated by genuine causal isolation. The target dismisses causal isolation without argument, simply asserting that heavy tails 'ensure' dominance regardless of topology. That is a bare assertion that assumes its conclusion.","counterexample":[{"distinguishing_evidence":"Pooled incident reports across operators that show no shared root cause after forensic investigation, combined with independent regional hazard modeling, is evidence of true independence — not merely hidden correlation.","scenario":"Two decentralized services in different regions fail simultaneously for unrelated causes. Shared-cause investigation finds no common root. Network remains partially available via surviving operators. The centralized system, had a comparable single cause hit its single site, would be fully down. The shared cause (site-level event) did not dominate the distributed topology because of genuine causal isolation from geographic separation."}],"target":"c7ae1fabedc08c45ac1c396e20eab1063f3ac659ede9f70a3a56b595835edaad"}]}